,{"td":6320,":@":6323},[6321],{"#text":6322},"5.68",{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1345},{"#text":1345},{"tr":6327},[6328,6329,6334,6335,6340,6341,6346,6347,6351,6352,6361,6362,6366],{"#text":1349},{"td":6330,":@":6333},[6331],{"#text":6332},"Our method",{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1356},{"#text":1349},{"td":6336,":@":6339},[6337],{"#text":6338},"2020",{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"td":6342,":@":6345},[6343],{"#text":6344},"89.2",{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"td":6348,":@":6350},[6349],{"#text":6344},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"td":6353,":@":6360},[6354,6355,6359],{"#text":1434},{"bold":6356},[6357],{"#text":6358},"99.9",{"#text":1349},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"td":6363,":@":6365},[6364],{"#text":1468},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1345},{"#text":1283},{"#text":817},{"@_frame":1475},{"#text":817},{"table-wrap-foot":6372},[6373,6374,6381],{"#text":1283},{"fn":6375},[6376,6377,6380],{"#text":1345},{"p":6378},[6379],{"#text":1486},{"#text":1283},{"#text":817},{"#text":823},{"@_id":5410,"@_position":1298},{"#text":823},{"p":6386},[6387],{"#text":6388},"Most state-of-the-art methods ensemble the segmentation results of multiple models, and the segmentation results of ensemble of multiple models is usually better than a single one. In order to show the performance of our proposed method more visual, we did not use the ensemble of multiple models, but only used the proposed single model to compare with other methods. For the whole brain tumor segmentation task, the Dice score of whole tumors reached 0.86-0.90, the Sensitivity score of whole tumors reached 0.85-0.92. Specificity scores of all methods are very high, almost over 0.99. The Hausdorff distance is basically between 4 and 7. The experimental results show that our method has a strong competitiveness.",{"#text":823},{"p":6391},[6392,6394,6402,6404,6412],{"#text":6393},"In order to make the comparison result more objective, we retrain several state-of-the-art segmentation models to the brain tumor dataset and evaluated them on the BraTS2020 dataset. It can be seen from ",{"xref":6395,":@":6400},[6396],{"bold":6397},[6398],{"#text":6399},"Table 6",{"@_ref-type":1268,"@_rid":6401},"T6",{"#text":6403}," that our method has achieved the first place in the DSC, Sensitivity, Specificity, and Hausdorff distance. At the same time, our method has the least number of parameters. ",{"xref":6405,":@":6410},[6406],{"bold":6407},[6408],{"#text":6409},"Figure 5",{"@_ref-type":1231,"@_rid":6411},"f5",{"#text":6413}," shows a more intuitive comparison between the segmentation results of our method and state-of-the-art methods.",{"#text":823},{"table-wrap":6416,":@":6821},[6417,6418,6421,6422,6430,6431,6808,6809,6820],{"#text":817},{"label":6419},[6420],{"#text":6399},{"#text":817},{"caption":6423},[6424,6425,6429],{"#text":1283},{"p":6426},[6427],{"#text":6428},"The results of comparison between our proposed method and state-of-the-art methods on the BraTS 2020.",{"#text":817},{"#text":817},{"table":6432,":@":6807},[6433,6434,6472,6473,6806],{"#text":1283},{"thead":6435},[6436,6437,6471],{"#text":1345},{"tr":6438},[6439,6440,6444,6445,6449,6450,6454,6455,6459,6460,6464,6465,6470],{"#text":1349},{"th":6441,":@":6443},[6442],{"#text":1353},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1356},{"#text":1349},{"th":6446,":@":6448},[6447],{"#text":1361},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"th":6451,":@":6453},[6452],{"#text":1368},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"th":6456,":@":6458},[6457],{"#text":1374},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"th":6461,":@":6463},[6462],{"#text":1380},{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1349},{"th":6466,":@":6469},[6467],{"#text":6468},"Parameter ",{"@_valign":1355,"@_align":1363},{"#text":1345},{"#text":1283},{"#text":1283},{"tbody":6474},[6475,6476,6519,6520,6566,6567,6612,6613,6659,6660,6706,6707,6750,6751,6805],{"#text":1345},{"tr"